# Build configuration for the usv-sitl project: Ubuntu 22.04 with the apt
# dependencies of ArduPilot Rover SITL, for the usv-autopilot SITL setup guide
# (Field-Robotics-Lab/usv-autopilot, usv-sitl/docs/getting-started/). Sourced
# by the drydock script.
#
# BASE_IMAGE   plain Ubuntu, not ros:*; this project has its own Dockerfile.
# DRYDOCK_HOME the home the container sees, in place of your own: the folder
#              this drydock checkout is cloned into, i.e. the guide's working
#              directory, which also holds the ardupilot and usv-autopilot
#              clones. They appear at the same paths inside the container, and
#              what ArduPilot's install script writes to ~ (pip --user into
#              ~/.local, ~/.bashrc, ~/.ardupilot_env) lands there as hidden
#              files, not in your real home. Do not clone drydock directly into
#              your home directory for this project.
#
# ROS_DISTRO is unused, but the drydock script exports it either way.

ROS_DISTRO=none
BASE_IMAGE=ubuntu:22.04
DRYDOCK_HOME="$(dirname "${HERE}")"
